agonist  is both a villain and a hero someone  willing to kill millions of innocent  people no matter what his reason may be  can definitely be classified as a  villain at the same time  from the subjective perspective of the  aldeans and parodies  aaron can also be seen as a hero and  that is exactly how the jaegerists see  him  this is because the jaegerists believe  much like aaron seems to believe  that destroying the outside world is the  only way to protect themselves  and literally everyone they ever loved  and cared about  it's either destroyed the world or be  destroyed  by it aaron appears to have chosen to  take upon himself  the horrible burden of killing millions  so that the aliens on the island could  live in peace  he will take all the guilt and all the  blame  while ensuring the survival of the  islanders by any means  necessary this shocking character  development that aaron has undergone  since the beginning of the story  is as incredible as it is tragic  to achieve his lifelong goals of being  free  and protecting his loved ones aaron had  to become  everything that he hated aaron is now in  a position  where he has to put millions of innocent  civilians through the same tragedy and  trauma that he himself was put through  as a child and he has to take all that  guilt and all that blame onto himself so  that his loved ones on parodies could  finally  live in peace what an amazing personal  story  and yet what a deeply tragic story at  the same time  no matter what ultimately happens in  attack on titan and no matter what aaron  ultimately decides to do  he is already one of the most  fascinating characters in the history of  anime for me  personally it's hard to imagine any  character undergoing such a drastic  shift throughout the story and yet  somehow still remaining true to his  original goals  and convictions a big part of why this  works  is of course the cruel nature of the  attack on titan world  a world where you pretty much have to be  