aron releases the walled titans and  takes on a new  absolutely gigantic and terrifying titan  form  aaron then leads this army of colossal  titans  into a massive attack on the military  forces of marley  and the other allied nations who had  assembled the world's most  powerful war fleet a fleet whose  intention was to destroy  parodies although his first target is  the fleet  it is generally understood that aaron's  plan is to flatten the entire  outside world unless aaron is secretly  planning something else that we are not  aware of  we can assume that after destroying the  enemy armed forces  he will continue to destroy everything  in sight  including of course innocent civilians  who have done nothing wrong  with this aaron's character has come  full  circle aaron has gone from a young boy  who swore to kill  every single titan in order to rescue  humanity to the leader of a titan  army whose goal is the destruction of  humanity  or at least the vast majority of  humanity  and yet through all of this staggering  character development  and it is definitely one of the most  impressive examples of character  development  in anime and manga aaron has remained  consistent  in terms of his personality and his  life's purpose  despite going from someone who wanted to  save humanity from the titans to someone  who is apparently determined to destroy  most of humanity with the help of the  titans aaron has not  become a hypocrite aaron is still driven  by the same  basic desires as he was when he was a  child  he just wants to be free and he just  wants to protect  the people he loves when he was younger  in the first part of the story  seeking freedom and protecting his loved  ones meant that aaron had to fight the  titans  in this second part of the story the  older and more mature  aaron realizes that the only way to be  free and protect his loved ones on  parodies  is to annihilate the outside world using  the titans  in that sense aaron who is of course the  protagonist  is both a villain and a hero someone  willing to kill millions of innocent  people no matter what his reason may be  can definitely be classified as a  villain at the same time  from the subjective perspective of the  aldeans and parodies  aaron can also be seen as a hero and  that is exactly how the jaegerists see  him  this is because the jaegerists believe  much like aaron seems to believe  that destroying the outside world is the  only way to protect themselves  and literally everyone they ever loved  and cared about  it's either destroyed the world or be  destroyed  by it aaron appears to have chosen to  take upon himself  the horrible burden of killing millions  so that the aliens on the island could  live in peace  he will take all the guilt and all the  blame  while ensuring the survival of the  islanders by any means  necessary this shocking character  development that aaron has undergone  since the beginning of the story  is as incredible as it is tragic  to achieve his lifelong goals of being  free  and protecting his loved ones aaron had  to become  everything that he hated aaron is now in  a position  where he has to put millions of innocent  civilians through the same tragedy and  trauma that he himself was put through  as a child and he has to take all that  guilt and all that blame onto himself so  that his loved ones on parodies could  finally  live in peace what an amazing personal  story  and yet what a deeply tragic story at  the same time  no matter what ultimately happens in  attack on titan and no matter what aaron  ultimately decides to do  he is already one of the most  fascinating characters in the history of  anime for me  personally it's hard to imagine any  character undergoing such a drastic  shift throughout the story and yet  somehow still remaining true to his  original goals  and convictions a big part of why this  works  is of course the cruel nature of the  attack on titan world  a world where you pretty much have to be  a villain to some  in order to be a hero to others and the  other part of it is the amazing way in  which isayama has written aaron as a  character  allowing him to develop in shocking and  unbelievable ways  while still remaining true to his inner  core aaron's  incredible and yet tragic character  progression  is one of the most powerful aspects of  attack on titan  and it is my belief that when everything  is said and done aaron will become one  of the most  memorable anime and manga characters on  par with the likes of lelouch  meruem like yagami simone from guren  lagon  and guts from berserk definitely let me  know what you guys think about the  tragic life of aaron  and his shocking character development  down in the comments below  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more videos like it please leave  a like to let me know  it really does help and if you're new to  anime  pro or you just haven't subscribed make  this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on all  notifications you can also hit me up on  twitter  and instagram at anime uproar  i want to give a big thank you to all of  our anime upper patrons for making  videos like this one possible special  thanks to all of our  the one tier patrons the ones who rise  above  all other clans including ingrata alolan  adam the world  steelers acquired respect pate heffa  jonathan king  brandon aviles papa smurf the school bus  king riser emperor otaku ricardo  martinez  thomas jones kin mano michael hyde  and jaden the vector and i can't forget  all of our pro hero tier patrons  including the one and only gilgamesh  nothing but a fan  jason wilson kings eldris and anatoly  kazatsky  on hell cruise cricket xp joe stanton  very gucci alicia octor jessica kayla  fond  hinokami and water bonnie parks zodiac  12  rathune de ora kraken rls and  deadly saint if you enjoy our videos and  you feel that they provide value to you  please consider supporting us on patreon  even a s